    },
    {
      "text": "it also actually goes to show how we really should be thinking about all these stages synergistically",
      "timestamp_sec": 929,
      "why": "Argues against the common org split between pre-, mid-, and post-training teams."
    },
    {
      "text": "if you hear this story over and over again, oh, if I want to customize a model, it's going to cost hundreds of millions of dollars",
      "timestamp_sec": 1010,
      "why": "Sets up the talk's cost-debunking claim."
    },
    {
      "text": "you can train an immensely powerful model especially in a narrow domain for high six figures million dollars. It's very doable to get a model that's extremely performant.",
      "timestamp_sec": 1047,
      "why": "Puts a concrete price range on custom model training."
    },
    {
      "text": "it's almost always better to repeat highquality data than it is to show lowquality data",
      "timestamp_sec": 1047,
      "why": "A directly actionable heuristic that cuts against pure token-count maximization."
    },
    {
      "text": "If you're sitting in a world where you want to build a model or customize a model and you're limited on compute, how do you get past that? Invest in data",
      "timestamp_sec": 1080,
      "why": "The closing prescription, stated as an explicit alternative to buying more compute."
    }
